    PM--Stokes  & 4.00 & $19.04\pm2.34$ & $17.35\pm1.78$ & 10 \\
    PM--Stokes  & 8.50 & $26.88\pm1.11$ & $26.49\pm1.33$ & 10 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

The directed RMS can be much larger than the scenario-level circular
mean error.  Wrong travel-sense decisions produce errors
near $180^\circ$ and therefore carry large quadratic weight in RMS, even
though the truth-referenced travel-sense decision is correct for
\OUValidationTravelCorrect\% of samples.  Reporting both metrics prevents the
aggregate correct-decision fraction from hiding large sense-flip errors.

